    /// <summary>
    /// A vertex moved of a closed multiline MLEDIT has cut (<c>DxfMlineBuilder.MoveVertexAt</c>, which a grip and STRETCH use)
    /// against the records AutoCAD 2021 left, as <see cref="MlineMoveVertexClosedEndsTests"/> does it, for the six-sided
    /// staircase 0,0 100,0 100,50 50,50 50,100 0,100 and the eight-sided one 0,0 120,0 120,40 80,40 80,80 40,80 40,120 0,120,
    /// the square and the triangle, cut by CA or CS across each vertex and one vertex moved by 8 to 20. A cut whose picks lie
    /// beyond the end of a mitred element (the stretch of the inner element at a concave corner is shorter than the path) takes
    /// nothing out of it, and is written as the element whole. A move that shortens a segment until a cut that reaches its end
    /// starts at the end leaves that stop out (the element is drawn to the end) and the list that goes on across the next vertex
    /// gets a nought in front, where a move that carries the start of a cut that goes on across a vertex back past the start of
    /// the segment leaves the list at nought and not a start of nought twice or a start below it.
    /// </summary>
